// The resources of nkb-gui.exe, as a script for `build.rs` to compile: the
// program's icon, and the file's details - version, author, licence. Nothing
// else goes in, no manifest - the point of the crate that compiles this is that
// it adds exactly what this file says.
//
// The details are written at build time from the package manifest, by
// crates/nkb-cli/file_details.rs, into the build's output directory, which the
// build script hands the compiler as a place to look for includes.
//
// The block is UTF-8 and says so, but the compiler honours a code page only in
// the script it was asked to compile, never in an included one - Microsoft's
// documentation of the pragma says so, and the compiler of an older Windows
// SDK, which the build picks when it finds one first, does what it says: the
// copyright sign came out as two letters. So the code page is named here,
// before the include.
#pragma code_page(65001)
#include "details.rc"

// The path is relative to this file. Resource 1 is the first icon group, and
// the first one is the icon Windows shows for the file.
1 ICON "edamame.ico"
